 last thing I wanted  to touch on was this issue of the  corporations that benefit from hiring  undocumented immigrants that has been  effectively missing from the discussion  obviously the president lobbying for his  wall is going to scapegoat undocumented  immigrants as the ones responsible for  holding down wages but you don't read  here a serious critique from either side  about the reality that it's the  corporations that are basically going  unpunished for hiring undocumented labor  that are really the driving force  between a behind a lot of that hiring  and wages is there just no political  appetite to to open up that can of worms  okay that's an interesting point you  know there is this idea of Eve Arif I  that would sort of require employers to  verify the immigrant status of workers  that they hire sort of electronically  against the database yeah the business  community has been notable notably  reticent about that Democrats you know  have been somewhat cool to that as well  as a result it really hasn't gotten very  far and you know it's a little hard for  me to sort of probe exactly why that is  we do know this that the structure of  our economy has changed dramatically in  the last 50 years we've seen a huge  growth in the service sector and  particularly in those parts of the  service sector that that do depend on  low skilled labor whether it's whether  its yard work you know lawn servicing  and landscape whether it's restaurant  the kind of service workers in  restaurants whether it's you know  construction I mean they're the demand  for unskilled labor the kinds of jobs  that immigrants are primed to fill has  really grown a lot and that may be why  you know you're not seeing a lot of  corporations or businesses right now  leading the charge against undocumented  workers because you know they are  employing them no question about it  we've been speaking with Tom Shelton  who's the religion and belief  correspondent for NPR news we're linking  to his book a nation of Nations a great  American immigration to a story Tom  thank you so much for talking to me it's  been really interesting thank you David

